My guess is that something has happened to your '/etc/securettys' file.=

Normally, it has the following entries in it to allow console and CDE
logins
as root:

    /dev/console
    local:0
    :0

Without those, you'll be unable to login as root.  And unless you're ro=
ot,
you can't edit that file to correct it.  The best thing to do is to boo=
t
into single user mode and correct the file.  Unless you're familiar wit=
h
the
'ed' editor, you may need to brush up; I believe that is the only edito=
r
available in single user mode.

